<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valdemar IV of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1320–1375</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Valdemar Atterdag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valdemar IV, known as Valdemar Atterdag, was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1340 to 1375 and rebuilt the kingdom after years in which its provinces had been pawned to foreign lords, recovering Zealand, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a> and other lands. In 1361 he invaded Gotland and took Visby, provoking war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>, which forced him to accept the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stralsund">Stralsund</a> in 1370. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I</a> later founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valdemar-iv-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Valdemar IV of Denmark" width="320" height="489" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown contemporary 14th-century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waldemar_IV_Otherday_of_Denmark_c_1375_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The great test came when <b>Valdemar IV of Denmark</b> sacked Visby in 1361 and defeated a Hanseatic fleet at Helsingborg in 1362.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League · Military</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Valdemar IV Atterdag</b> sacked Visby on Gotland in 1361 but lost the ensuing war with the Hanseatic League, ended by the Treaty of Stralsund in 1370.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-denmark">Kingdom of Denmark · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The St George's Night Uprising of 1343 persuaded the Danish crown that its Estonian lands were too costly to hold, and in 1346 <b>Valdemar IV</b> sold them to the Teutonic Order, which entrusted them to its Livonian branch.</blockquote><a href="/empire/reval">Reval · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In the north, German trading towns led by Lübeck formed the Hanseatic League, whose victory over <b>Valdemar IV of Denmark</b>, sealed by the Treaty of Stralsund in 1370, marked the height of its power.</blockquote><a href="/government/city-state">City-state · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>The Livonian Order crushed the revolt, and in 1346 <b>Valdemar IV</b> sold the duchy to the Teutonic Order, which handed it to its Livonian branch.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-estonia-1219-1346">Duchy of Estonia (1219-1346)</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1361 <b>Valdemar IV of Denmark</b> invaded, massacring the farmers' army outside Visby.</blockquote><a href="/state/gotland">Gotland</a></li></ul></section>
